WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.400
LABSPACE brings children and grown-ups together around a small scientific question. These are real application

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:10.800
captures. No child account, public profile or date of birth is needed.

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:16.800
Make a prediction, then launch the same ball on Earth and the Moon. A deterministic

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:22.800
physics engine calculates both paths on a shared scale. A wrong first guess is welcome.

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:28.200
The youngest children choose simple push buttons with a grown-up. Older explorers use more precise

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:33.600
controls and measurements. Motion, pendulums and additive light each have documented assumptions.

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:39.200
Keep a prediction, the calculated result and a personal observation in a local notebook. Reopen

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:44.800
the experiment with the same settings. Discoveries stay in this browser unless exported.

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:48.933
Create together selects a reviewed activity. By default this uses prewritten activities, clearly labeled. Optional

00:00:48.933 --> 00:00:53.067
AI may select an allowed module and preset; it never invents physics or executes generated

00:00:53.067 --> 00:00:57.200
code.

00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:02.200
The science functions, persistence and browser journeys are tested. This is a virtual laboratory, with

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:07.200
simplified models and explicit limits. Little questions. Big discoveries. Together.
